fix(reaper): sweep the runs the ledger calls active with no SPIRE entry (#289)

The reaper's population was the SPIRE entry list; the ledger's `active` is
the absence of `run_retired`/`run_expired`. Measured: the ledger held four
active runs, SPIRE held entries for three, and the fourth could never be
expired whatever its state. The report said "3 live" beside a ledger of four.

The SET is widened; the DECISION is not touched. An unentried run is judged by
the same `orphaned` predicate, over the same last activity, with the same
grace. No threshold is added. A working run with no entry stays live, and that
control is SPI-018's whole table.

Reconciled rather than driven from the ledger, because driving it from the
ledger loses AB-11: an entry the ledger never heard of is a planted identity,
and only the SPIRE side can see it.

The report's second line now says what the sweep did not look at, so a count
of entries no longer reads as a count of agents.

